      {
        "id": 114739,
        "name": "Objulen",
        "username": "Objulen",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/o/779978/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-11-27T13:48:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>A better comparison would be Dark Watch Visionary.</p><p>Getting closer to the bad cards is only an issue if stop stacking the villain deck.</p><p>And it is situational, but Writhe's power is so situational that it's hard to justify. I can see possibly using it to duck some nasty surprises, but you are just as likely to hurt yourself as help yourself when using it with the villain deck.&nbsp;</p>",
